# Hyperliquid exporter configuration, installed at /etc/default/hyperliquid-exporter.
# Juju deployments: the principal Hyperliquid charm manages this file.
# Standalone deployments: edit it, then restart hyperliquid-exporter.service.
# APT preserves edits to this conffile on upgrade.
#
# Use systemd EnvironmentFile syntax: NAME=value, without "export".
# Values do not expand shell variables: use absolute paths, not $HOME or ~.
# See /usr/share/doc/hyperliquid-metrics-exporter/README.packaging for all flags.

# Network: mainnet or testnet. The service passes this as --chain.
CHAIN=mainnet

# Existing node data directory. The exporter only needs read/search access.
# Defaults match the Hyperliquid charm; change these for a custom runtime home.
NODE_HOME=/home/hyperliquid/hl

# Existing hl-node executable used for local node version metrics, not hl-visor.
NODE_BINARY=/home/hyperliquid/hl-node

# Directory containing hl-visor for --binary-metrics version checks.
# Also supplies the NODE_BINARY fallback if NODE_BINARY is unset/empty.
BINARY_HOME=/home/hyperliquid

# Writable exporter persistence: --peer-latency stores peers.json here.
# Keep the package default, which APT provisions and the unit permits writing.
EXPORTER_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/hyperliquid-exporter

# Extra "start" flags. Empty retains the application's monitor defaults.
# Use --flag=false to disable a boolean, not "--flag false".
# Keep chain and node paths in the variables above rather than repeating flags.
EXPORTER_ARGS=

# Optional monitor example, off by default:
# EXPORTER_ARGS="--evm-metrics --replica-metrics --peer-latency"
# --evm-metrics: EVM blocks/receipts and accounts.
# --replica-metrics: transactions parsed from replica_cmds.
# --validator-rtt: validator IP/RTT monitoring.
# --peer-latency: TCP probes to known peers, with persistent peer history.
# --binary-metrics: compare local hl-visor to the published binary over the network.
#
# Local monitor switches, on by default; use =false to disable:
# --process-metrics: hl-node/hl-visor process liveness and resource usage.
# --child-stderr-metrics: hl-visor child crash artifacts.
# --visor-metrics: visor sync state.
# --node-state-metrics: persisted checkpoint/freeze heights.
# --disk-metrics: node directory sizes and filesystem capacity.
# --operator-config-metrics: validator operator configuration.
# --crit-msg-metrics: bug!/crit! counts and locations.
#
# Logging example: debug, info (default), warning or error.
# EXPORTER_ARGS="--log-level=debug"
#
# OTLP/HTTP example. --otlp needs --otlp-endpoint, --alias and a configured CHAIN.
# EXPORTER_ARGS="--otlp --otlp-endpoint=collector.example:4318 --alias=my-node"
# Add --otlp-insecure only for an HTTP collector. TLS is the default.
# These are alternate examples: combine desired flags into one EXPORTER_ARGS.
# HOME is supplied by the unit as /var/lib/hyperliquid-exporter; leave it unchanged.
